From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: fsoc2: add Fortinet FortiSOC2 platform

The FortiSOC2 is the SoC of the Fortinet FortiGate 60D appliance, the
successor of the FortiSOC1. It is a Faraday FA726TE core, handled like an
ARM926EJ-S, with stock Faraday peripherals (FTINTC010, FTTMR010,
FTUART010, FTWDT010), all supported by existing drivers.

Like ARCH_FSOC1, the platform needs no mach- directory: the generic DT
machine descriptor is enough, so this only adds the Kconfig symbol. It
depends on ARCH_MULTI_V5, as the core is an ARMv5TE.

The stock boot loader passes ATAGs and cannot load a device tree, so a
bootable kernel needs ARM_APPENDED_DTB and ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT. As for the
FortiSOC1, these are left to the kernel configuration.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/Kconfig.platforms | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/Kconfig.platforms
+++ b/arch/arm/Kconfig.platforms
@@ -104,6 +104,23 @@ config ARCH_FSOC1
 	  ATAGs, so a kernel for this platform needs ARM_APPENDED_DTB and
 	  ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT.
 
+config ARCH_FSOC2
+	bool "Fortinet FortiSOC2"
+	depends on ARCH_MULTI_V5
+	depends on CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN
+	select CPU_ARM926T
+	select FARADAY_FTINTC010
+	select FTTMR010_TIMER
+	help
+	  Support for the Fortinet FortiSOC2, found in the FortiGate 60D
+	  appliance. It is built around a Faraday FA726TE core and stock
+	  Faraday peripherals: FTINTC010 interrupt controller, FTTMR010
+	  timer, FTUART010 serial ports and FTWDT010 watchdog.
+
+	  The stock boot loader cannot pass a device tree. It only passes
+	  ATAGs, so a kernel for this platform needs ARM_APPENDED_DTB and
+	  ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT.
+
 menuconfig ARCH_HPE
 	bool "HPE SoC support"
 	depends on ARCH_MULTI_V7
